Input: {"question": "Which person or organization did Danny T Huang work for?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 17, "text": "**Danny T Huang**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 19, "end": 120, "text": "Danny T Huang is a researcher who has made significant contributions to the field of cancer research."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 121, "end": 131, "text": "**Career**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 133, "end": 236, "text": "Huang has worked at several esteemed institutions, including the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 237, "end": 278, "text": "**Beatson Institute for Cancer Research**"}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 280, "end": 387, "text": "The Beatson Institute for Cancer Research is a leading cancer research center located in Glasgow, Scotland."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 388, "end": 519, "text": "The institute is a part of the University of Glasgow and is recognized for its cutting-edge research in cancer biology and therapy."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 520, "end": 578, "text": "**Evidence of Huang's Affiliation with Beatson Institute**"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 580, "end": 732, "text": "According to Huang's profile on the University of Glasgow's website, he was a researcher at the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research from 2010 to 2015."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 733, "end": 889, "text": "[1] During his tenure, he was involved in several research projects focused on understanding the molecular mechanisms of cancer development and progression."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 890, "end": 1031, "text": "A publication in the journal _Cancer Research_ in 2013 lists Huang as a co-author and affiliate of the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1032, "end": 1194, "text": "[2] The study, which investigated the role of a specific protein in cancer cell proliferation, was conducted in collaboration with researchers from the institute."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1195, "end": 1331, "text": "Additionally, Huang's LinkedIn profile also lists his affiliation with the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research during the same period."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1332, "end": 1335, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1337, "end": 1351, "text": "**References**"}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1353, "end": 1379, "text": "[1] University of Glasgow."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1380, "end": 1387, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1388, "end": 1402, "text": "Danny T Huang."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1403, "end": 1497, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.gla.ac.uk\\/research\\/expertise\\/expertsearch\\/?expert_id=123456>"}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1499, "end": 1512, "text": "[2] Huang, D."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1513, "end": 1523, "text": "T., et al."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1524, "end": 1531, "text": "(2013)."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1532, "end": 1624, "text": "\"Protein X regulates cancer cell proliferation through modulation of the PI3K\\/AKT pathway.\""}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1625, "end": 1660, "text": "Cancer Research, 73(11), 3321-3332."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1661, "end": 1696, "text": "doi: 10.1158\\/0008-5472.CAN-12-3456"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1698, "end": 1711, "text": "[3] LinkedIn."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1712, "end": 1719, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1720, "end": 1734, "text": "Danny T Huang."}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1735, "end": 1797, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.linkedin.com\\/in\\/dannythuang\\/>"}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1799, "end": 1945, "text": "This Wikipedia entry provides comprehensive evidence to support the claim that Danny T Huang worked for the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research."}, "D1S31": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1946, "end": 2098, "text": "The evidence includes Huang's profile on the University of Glasgow's website, a publication in a reputable scientific journal, and his LinkedIn profile."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 101, "text": "**Breakthrough Researcher Danny T Huang Leaves Lasting Impact at Ben-Gurion University of the Negev**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 103, "end": 347, "text": "Beersheba, Israel - In a career spanning over a decade, renowned researcher Danny T Huang has made significant contributions to the scientific community, with a substantial portion of his work taking place at Ben-Gurion University of the Negev."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 348, "end": 504, "text": "Huang's groundbreaking research has left an indelible mark on the institution, earning him recognition as one of the university's most distinguished alumni."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 505, "end": 645, "text": "During his tenure at Ben-Gurion University, Huang focused on cutting-edge projects in the fields of biotechnology and environmental science."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 646, "end": 776, "text": "His work on sustainable energy solutions and innovative approaches to waste management has been widely cited and praised by peers."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 777, "end": 833, "text": "\"Danny's dedication to his craft is inspiring,\" said Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 834, "end": 917, "text": "Rachel Cohen, Dean of the Faculty of Engineering Sciences at Ben-Gurion University."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 918, "end": 1098, "text": "\"His research has not only advanced our understanding of complex environmental issues but has also paved the way for practical applications that can benefit communities worldwide.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1099, "end": 1247, "text": "Huang's most notable achievement during his time at the university was the development of a novel system for converting organic waste into biofuels."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1248, "end": 1406, "text": "This pioneering work, published in the prestigious journal Nature Sustainability, has been hailed as a game-changer in the quest for renewable energy sources."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1407, "end": 1549, "text": "\"I was fortunate to have had the opportunity to work with an exceptional team at Ben-Gurion University,\" Huang said in an exclusive interview."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1550, "end": 1708, "text": "\"The university's commitment to interdisciplinary research and its state-of-the-art facilities provided the ideal environment for me to explore and innovate.\""}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1709, "end": 1879, "text": "According to data from the university, Huang's research has resulted in over 50 publications in top-tier scientific journals, with a cumulative impact factor of over 200."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1880, "end": 2022, "text": "His work has also led to the filing of several patents, with multiple companies already expressing interest in commercializing his inventions."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2023, "end": 2148, "text": "\"Danny's contributions to our institution have been immense,\" said Professor Chaim Hames, President of Ben-Gurion University."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2149, "end": 2303, "text": "\"We are proud to have had him as a member of our academic community and look forward to seeing the continued impact of his research in the years to come.\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2304, "end": 2481, "text": "As Huang moves on to new challenges, his legacy at Ben-Gurion University of the Negev remains a testament to the institution's commitment to fostering innovation and excellence."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Danny T Huang", "scope": "organization", "claim": "Danny T Huang worked for the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research.", "answer": "Beatson Institute for Cancer Research", "quote": "According to Huang's profile on the University of Glasgow's website, he was a researcher at the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research from 2010 to 2015. [1] During his tenure, he was involved in several research projects focused on understanding the molecular mechanisms of cancer development and progression. A publication in the journal _Cancer Research_ in 2013 lists Huang as a co-author and affiliate of the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research. [2] The study, which investigated the role of a specific protein in cancer cell proliferation, was conducted in collaboration with researchers from the institute. Additionally, Huang's LinkedIn profile also lists his affiliation with the Beatson Institute for Cancer Research during the same period.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c1", "entity": "Danny T Huang", "scope": "organization", "claim": "Danny T Huang worked for Ben-Gurion University.", "answer": "Ben-Gurion University", "quote": "\"I was fortunate to have had the opportunity to work with an exceptional team at Ben-Gurion University,\" Huang said in an exclusive interview. \"The university's commitment to interdisciplinary research and its state-of-the-art facilities provided the ideal environment for me to explore and innovate.\"", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Beatson Institute for Cancer Research", "Ben-Gurion University"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Beatson Institute for Cancer Research", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Ben-Gurion University", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
